spark-zap.mp3 is an original sound synthesized for sparkdock with ffmpeg. It is
not derived from any third-party work and carries no external license.

It is a 700 ms rising sine sweep (110 Hz climbing) layered over a 60 Hz sub-bass
with a 120 Hz harmonic, with an exponential decay and a low-pass roll-off.

Reproduce with:

ffmpeg -y -f lavfi -i "aevalsrc=0.85*(0.45*sin(2*PI*(110*t+421*t*t))+0.4*sin(2*PI*60*t)+0.2*sin(2*PI*120*t))*exp(-3.5*t)*min(1\,t/0.01):d=0.7:s=44100" -af "lowpass=f=2200" -ac 1 -b:a 96k spark-zap.mp3
